  m_Name: Blade5
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Rear Blade Upper
  description: The Rear Blade Upper is a stationary blade located at the rear of
    the engine, positioned above the Rear Blade Left and Right. It plays a crucial
    role in directing the flow of gases and maintaining engine efficiency, and works
    in conjunction with other rear blades to ensure a smooth flow of gases and minimize
    energy losses. One interesting detail is that the Rear Blade Upper is often designed
    with a unique shape to accommodate the engine's exhaust nozzle.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 8300000, guid: f99473c876ea79043942dc6beee26a4e, type: 3}
